SUMMARY:Home Is Where the Identity Is: Self Expression within Historic Interiors
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Beauport\, the Sleeper-McCann House\, the summer cottage of one of America’s first professional interior designers\, Henry Davis Sleeper. \nUnder the guidance of a historian\, explore the grand social spaces and intimate private rooms of this intact historic residence to get to know Sleeper\, a gay man living in the early twentieth century. \nUnpack the floorplan and examine architectural devices in this domestic interior to discover aspects of Sleeper’s identity\, ranging from his professional practice\, social engagements\, and sexuality. \nPresented by researcher and historian Dr. Hillary Walker. All are welcome. No registration necessary.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/home-is-where-the-identity-is-self-expression-within-historic-interiors/
LOCATION:Danforth Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 5P2
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
